          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral perturbation theory
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclear+physics"} nuclear physics
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            sector, where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            are
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadrons"} hadrons
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+meson"} light
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+mesons"} scalar mesons
                appear as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goldstone+bosons"} Goldstone bosons
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} spontaneously broken
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry"} chiral symmetry
                (see below),
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
                appear as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
                of a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hidden+local+symmetry"} hidden local symmetry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
                (specifically
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclei"} nuclei
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solitons"} solitons
                in the meson-fields (called
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heavy+mesons"} heavy mesons
                appear as further
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
          %p
            Hence some authors also speak of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
          %p
            More concretely, chiral perturbation theory is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbation theory
            not in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constant"} coupling constant
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/masses"} masses
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+quarks"} light quarks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/up+quark"} up quark
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/down+quark"} down quark
            and possibly also of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strange+quark"} strange quark
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_u
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_d
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_s
          %p
            As such, the point about which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbations
            are considered in chiral perturbation theory of QCD is that of vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark"} quark
            masses, hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+of+a+sequence"} limit
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_u, m_s, m_d \rightarrow 0
          %p#ProtonMass
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proton"} proton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            (the characteristic scale of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            witnessing its
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            = succeed "-property," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap"} mass gap
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "proton#Roberts21"} Roberts 21
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constituent+quarks"} constituent quarks
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi p
                  %mo ≫
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi u
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi d
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  m_p \gg 2 m_u + m_d
                  \\,,
          %p
            suggesting that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi u
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi d
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_u, m_d \to 0
            is a good limit around which to inspect the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadronic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
          %p#LagrangianInCPTLimit
            But since only the quark mass term in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            mixes the two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+spinor"} chiralities
            of quarks, its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            in this massless limit is the sum of a term that only contains the left-chiral quark spinors, and an analogous summand that only contains the right-chiral quark spinors (e.g.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Ecker95"} Ecker 95, (2.1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi QCD
                    %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi l
                      %mo =
                      %mi u
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi s
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mover
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi L
                    %mi l
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %menclose{:notation => "updiagonalstrike"}
                    %mi D
                  %mo +
                  %menclose{:notation => "updiagonalstrike"}
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msubsup
                    %mi q
                    %mi L
                    %mi l
                  %mo +
                  %msubsup
                    %mover
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi R
                    %mi l
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %menclose{:notation => "updiagonalstrike"}
                    %mi D
                  %mo +
                  %menclose{:notation => "updiagonalstrike"}
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msubsup
                    %mi q
                    %mi R
                    %mi l
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
